Package: enigma2-plugin-extensions-mqttbridge
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Section: extra
Priority: optional
Depends: python3-core, python3-json, python3-threading, python3-netclient
Maintainer: Damian Wilczek <deltasystems-pl@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/deltasystems-pl/enigma2-mqtt-bridge
License: GPL-2.0-or-later
Description: Push receiver state to MQTT and take commands back.
 Keeps one MQTT session to your broker and publishes the receiver's state the
 moment enigma2 raises the event - zap, EPG change, standby, recording, volume,
 remote key - instead of making a home-automation system poll OpenWebif.
 Commands travel back on the same session: power, zap, volume, mute, remote
 keys, on-screen messages, timers, recording and screenshots, each verified by
 effect. Announces itself with Home Assistant MQTT discovery, or stays quiet for
 the companion Home Assistant integration to build its own entities. Pure
 Python, no native code, no outbound connection other than your broker.
